  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186087700,
      "id": "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2",
      "title": "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b465be10-f95d-5020-9631-0d30bf0da972",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -17 & -7 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -17 & -7 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AC=CA={I}_{3}$\n- **II.** $AD=DA={I}_{3}$\n- **III.** $D={A}^{-1}$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- First, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -17 & -7 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -17 & -7 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AD=DA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -17 & -7 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\u2217 & \u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & 7 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217 & \u2217\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false. As a result, $D\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "be6eb58f-9268-553d-b9f1-965e43fea176",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
