  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186087700,
      "id": "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2",
      "title": "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "cfa60ceb-7aee-5afc-91a7-169414484ab8",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 5 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $AB=BA={I}_{3}$\n\nII. $AC=CA={I}_{3}$\n\nIII. $B={A}^{-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 5 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\u2217 & \u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & 7 & \u2217\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 5 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 5 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "965119df-310b-5a45-af41-9cb2343b1d02",
