  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186087700,
      "id": "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2",
      "title": "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a67bf168-9cac-5f3a-b870-9030d0ca52f9",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\frac{1}{15}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $BC=CB={I}_{3}$\n- **II.** $BD=DB={I}_{3}$\n- **III.** $D={B}^{-1}$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- First, we check whether $BC=CB={I}_{3}.$ Computing $BC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\frac{1}{15}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\u2217 & \u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217 & \\frac{1}{15}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false.\n\n- Note, we check whether $BD=DB={I}_{3}.$ Computing $BD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BD & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true. As a result, $D={B}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "cc51713f-721d-5d4e-b832-73e56fb964db",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
